<!--
  Sun and cloud.

  The sun sits clear of the cloud rather than behind it. Overlapped, the two shapes merged into
  one blob at the twenty-two points this is drawn at in a strip, which is what "primitive" looks
  like from arm's length. Separated, with the sun up and right and the cloud down and left, both
  are still legible at half that size.

  Only the five rays that point away from the cloud are drawn. The three that would point into it
  are the ones that made the blob, and a sun is recognisable from an arc of rays — it does not
  need the full eight to say what it is.
-->
